# i18n (next-intl v4 + locale routing)

## Layout

| Piece | Path |
|-------|------|
| Locales | `en` · `fa` in `src/i18n/routing.ts` (`defineRouting`) |
| Request | `src/i18n/request.ts` (plugin `./src/i18n/request.ts`; includes `timeZone`) |
| Navigation | `src/i18n/navigation.ts` |
| Proxy | `src/proxy.ts` (Next.js 16+; next-intl `createMiddleware`) |
| Messages | `messages/<locale>.json` |
| App routes | `src/app/[locale]/…` |
| Sample switcher | `src/app/_components/locale-switcher/` (homepage only) |

## Do

- Prefer `@/i18n/navigation` (`Link`, `useRouter`, `usePathname`) over `next/link` / `next/navigation`.
- Prefer `getTranslations` (Server) / `useTranslations` (Client) — avoid hardcoded UI copy when a key exists.
- New pages/layouts go under `src/app/[locale]/` (not `src/app/` root).
- Homepage samples stay in `src/app/_components/` (shared across locales) — never park them in `src/components/`.
- Keep `api/`, `globals.css`, sitemap/robots at `src/app/` root.
- Locale layout: `hasLocale` → `setRequestLocale` → `getMessages` + `getTimeZone` → pass `locale` + `messages` + `timeZone` into client `AppProviders` (`NextIntlClientProvider` does not inherit when nested under a Client Component).
- Keep a global `timeZone` in `src/i18n/request.ts` (default `UTC`) to avoid `ENVIRONMENT_FALLBACK` mismatches.
- Add a locale: extend `routing.locales` + add `messages/<locale>.json`.
- Keep `next-intl@^4.5` — v3 injects `experimental.turbo` which Next.js 16 rejects.

## Don't

- Put localized routes beside `[locale]` at `src/app/<page>` (proxy expects the locale prefix).
- Hardcode `/en/...` paths in links — use navigation helpers so locale switches stay correct.
- Rely on server→client message/timeZone inheritance without passing props into `AppProviders`.
- Use the deprecated `src/middleware.ts` file convention — Next.js 16 expects `src/proxy.ts`.
